  "limitations": [
    "Targeted automated tests; no full beginning-to-end playthrough on each emulator.",
    "Dungeon entry checks cover room 0 unless another room is explicitly listed.",
    "No claim that every custom NPC was visited on every core; V107 actor and asset binaries are byte-identical to V108.",
    "RMG is a Mupen64Plus frontend/fork distribution; ares is the independent emulator implementation.",
    "ares tests use the unchanged N64 static library from the v148 source release with a small automated frontend; the regular Qt desktop app was separately built and booted.",
    "Software Vulkan (Mesa lavapipe 25.0.7) and Mesa software OpenGL on Xvfb; these runs are not a real-hardware GPU performance measurement.",
    "Pieps/critical-room save contexts are seeded at the native Play_Init entry after a real file-menu load; accepted enemy-hit flags and a native bomb are driven by the harness. These are not manually played complete dungeon runs.",
    "The official Mupen 2.6.0 binary ran with its normal 8 MiB configuration; the RMG and ares cases explicitly used 4 MiB."
  ],
  "harness_corrections": [
    "Direct forced PlayState replacement from the old Mupen harness was not used as a compatibility result for the new packages. Native SRAM/menu loads replaced it.",
    "SRAM outdoors reloads were counted as Links House/Temple of Time, because Sram_OpenSave normally redirects to those scenes; they are not counted as Kokiri Forest visits.",
    "Initial official-package test expected 4 MiB but that binary actually allocated 8 MiB; final test explicitly expects its 8 MiB configuration.",
    "The first ares boss probe queried the new NPC in the same VI in which the cutscene state changed; the final probe waits up to 180 VIs for native actor initialization. The ROM was unchanged.",
    "Some opening probes had bounded runtimes and were not counted as full-intro passes. The separate official260 fresh-newfile test completed the entire opening."
  ]
